# Trims the build context. The image builds from the workspace root because
# wiretap-backend is a workspace member and cargo needs the root manifest and
# lockfile; the Dockerfile copies an explicit list, so this file is defence in
# depth rather than the mechanism.
#
# Docker matches these against the whole context-relative path and, unlike
# .gitignore, a slash-free pattern is NOT any-depth. Hence `**/` on everything
# that has to be excluded wherever it appears — `.env` alone would match only a
# root one, while the file the READMEs tell you to create is at
# crates/wiretap-backend/.env.

**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

.git/
.github/
**/.claude/
**/CLAUDE.md

**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt

# Not needed to build the image: appliance packaging, the Python oracle and
# admin tools, and the docs.
debian/
packaging/
tools/
docs/

**/*.deb
**/*.img
**/*.img.xz
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.DS_Store
